{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Also with me HaShem was angry because of you, etc.</b> On this verse most of the commentators set out to gather explanations and found no sufficient reason for how the decree against Moses was placed among the spies. See the Ramban and the Mahar'i'a and other commentators. And according to what we explained above in parashat Ḥukkat (Numbers 20:8) regarding the matter of the sin of the waters of Meribah: had Israel been sons in whom faith was firmly rooted and not men of little faith, Moses' punishment would not have been so great for failing to cause them to believe, as it is written (Numbers 20:12): ״יַעַן לֹא הֶאֱמַנְתֶּם״ — it was not said אֲמַנְתֶּם but rather ״הֶאֱמַנְתֶּם,״ which is the hif'il form outgoing to two, that is, you did not cause Israel to hold fast to faith; and who needs strengthening if not one who is among the men of little faith? But if from of old they had been strong in faith, there would have been no need at all to perform before them an act of miracles in order to strengthen their heart in faith. And even though it was already stated (Exodus 14:31): ״וַיַּאֲמִינוּ בַּה׳״ and so forth, none the less the spies caused them to revert to being sons in whom faith was not rooted, as Moses himself said regarding how he addressed them in the matter of the spies: ״וּבַדָּבָר הַזֶּה אֵינְכֶם מַאֲמִינִים בַּה׳״ and so forth. And the admission of a litigant is like one hundred witnesses, for Moses admitted that in the matter of the spies they became unbelieving. And all the more so should he have performed the matter of bringing forth water from the rock in such a manner that they would return to their former state in the matter of faith, and he did not do so; therefore it was decreed upon him not to enter there. Therefore he said after the verse ״וּבַדָּבָר הַזֶּה אֵינְכֶם מַאֲמִינִים בַּה׳״ and so forth — ״גַּם בִּי הִתְאַנַּף ה׳ בִּגְלַלְכֶם לֵאמֹר גַּם אַתָּה לֹא תָבֹא שָׁמָּה״: what is ״גַּם אַתָּה״? Just as the spies will not enter there on account of the fact that they do not believe in HaShem, as stated, so too you will not enter there for this very reason, as it is written: ״יַעַן לֹא הֶאֱמַנְתֶּם בִּי״ — for the sin of the many who lead them astray is suspended upon him." "Another matter: therefore he inserted here the decree of Moses, for this depends on that — for on account of the decree of the spies they were delayed in the wilderness forty years, and during this time the moment of Miriam's death arrived, and on account of this the well ceased upon her death and they lacked water, and the matter of the waters of Meribah rolled on because of this. And had the spies not sinned, they would have entered the land immediately together with Miriam, and Moses would not have come to the point of this punishment." "And regarding what is written ״בִּגְלַלְכֶם״ and he did not say ״בַּעֲבוּרְכֶם״, one may resolve it according to what our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 14a) that Moses was buried opposite Beth Pe'or in order to atone for the matter of Pe'or, for they would excrete dung against him — רְעִי וְגָלָל; therefore he said ״בִּגְלַלְכֶם״ from the language of ״כַּאֲשֶׁר יְבַעֵר הַגָּלָל״ (I Kings 14:10). And therefore ״גַּם אַתָּה״ is said to include even his bones, as Rashi explained on the verse ״הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי מֵת אֵינֶנִּי עוֹבֵר״ (Deuteronomy 4:22) — even my bones do not pass over — and all this in order to atone for the matter of Pe'or."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The abbreviation מהרי״א is resolved as Mahar'i'a, following common citation practice; it likely refers to Rabbi Isaac Arama (Akedat Yitzhak). The verse quotation in the lemma tail 'וגו׳' is rendered 'and so forth.' The address '(כ ח)' after 'פרשת חקת' appears to refer to Numbers 20:8, the passage on the waters of Meribah.", 2 "The Talmudic citation '(סוטה יד)' is resolved as Sotah 14a based on the well-known passage about Moses' burial opposite Beth Pe'or."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:11:37.912578059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}